Die offene Haelfte von karr #76 nach docs/adr/0041. Dort ist die SEQUENZ-Position geloest (Kommentar-Leaf wird erhalten); die MAPPING-Position ist es nicht, und zwar in beide Richtungen:

LESEN: sops schreibt einen Kommentar ueber einem Mapping-Key als echte
Kommentarzeile (#ENC[...,type:comment]). YAML::XS verwirft sie, bevor
Format::YAML::parse einen Baum sieht. Wir sehen den Kommentar also nie.

SCHREIBEN: YAML::XS kann ueberhaupt keinen Kommentar emittieren, also koennten
wir ihn auch nicht zurueckschreiben, wenn wir ihn haetten.

HARMLOS, aber verlustig: das Dokument liest sich korrekt (sops hasht den
Kommentar nicht, wir auch nicht), nur geht der Kommentar bei jedem
Schreibpfad verloren -- rotate, edit, encrypt_in_place, decrypt_file +
encrypt_file. Das war schon immer so und ADR 0024 wie ADR 0041 sagen es
ausdruecklich.

WAS ES BRAUCHT: einen Parser, der Kommentare erhaelt, UND einen Emitter, der
sie an den folgenden Knoten zurueckhaengt. YAML::PP kann das Erste nicht als
Baum-Feature; YAML::XS kann das Zweite gar nicht. Textchirurgie auf dem
fertigen Dokument ist die, die ADR 0019 abgelehnt hat (beliebiger Key-Pfad in
beliebiger Verschachtelung, auf dem Schreibpfad, ein Fehltreffer schreibt eine
kaputte Datei) -- ADR 0028s Bedingungen fuer erlaubte Textchirurgie erfuellt
sie in keinem Punkt.

Fuer JSON gibt es nichts zu tun: sops selbst verwirft Mapping-Kommentare beim
Schreiben nach JSON (gemessen, sops 3.13.3).

Lane: format, mit wire als Zweitleser -- ein erhaltener Kommentar muesste
denselben Platz im Baum bekommen, den ADR 0041 fuer die Sequenzposition
gebaut hat, und derselbe Digest-Ausschluss gilt.

MEASURED, NOT IMPLEMENTED -- and the ticket's two "no"s are both confirmed, one
of them for a stronger reason than the body gives. Nothing in lib/ changed for
this; the POD under Format::YAML::parse now carries the finding, and
docs/adr/0050 records it under "What this leaves open".

WHAT YAML::PP CAN REALLY DO (v0.41.0, the version this distribution loads):
  * Its LOADER cannot preserve comments. PRESERVE_ORDER, PRESERVE_SCALAR_STYLE,
    PRESERVE_FLOW_STYLE and PRESERVE_ALIAS are the whole preserve set -- there
    is no comment flag -- and YAML::PP's own POD lists a comment-preserving
    parse tree as a TODO ("I would like to generate a complete parse tree ...
    including all whitespaces and comments").
  * Its PARSER does keep the text. YAML::PP::Parser->tokens holds the comment
    inside EOL tokens -- measured, a three-comment document yields all three
    verbatim. So the READ half is mechanically reachable, which is more than
    the ticket body says. Two caveats: ->tokens is an undocumented accessor
    (YAML::PP::Parser has NO pod at all), and a token carries no attachment to
    a node, so correlating it with the event stream would be new machinery.

WHY THE READ HALF ALONE IS WORTHLESS HERE: there is nowhere to put a recovered
mapping-position comment. ADR 0041 could preserve a SEQUENCE comment because a
sequence element is a slot the tree model already has. A mapping-position
comment sits BEFORE a key, and a Perl hash has no slot before a key. Holding it
needs an ordered/annotated mapping model -- a data-model change, not a parser
change -- or the text surgery ADR 0019 and ADR 0041 both rejected.

THE WRITE HALF IS A WALL, NOT A LANE HANDOFF, and this is the part that settles
the ticket. It is not "our emitter lacks an option" (karr #99): NO emitter
available to this distribution can write a comment at all.
  * YAML::XS is libyaml, whose emitter has no comment concept.
  * YAML::PP::Emitter has no comment event either -- its event set is the
    standard YAML one (mapping/sequence/scalar/alias/document/stream), same
    TODO as above.
So even swapping the emitter -- which would be a wire change and the wire lane's
-- would not buy the write half. I did not touch the emitter.

NEW MEASUREMENT, sops 3.13.3, worth having on the record. sops writes a
mapping-position comment and a file-leading comment as `#ENC[...,type:comment]`
LINES and a sequence one as an ELEMENT; `sops -d` returns all of them intact.
Here the two positions behave DIFFERENTLY:
  * comment as a sequence element  -> decrypt_file/edit REFUSE the document,
    loudly, naming the path (ADR 0041's guard).
  * comment above a mapping key, and nothing else -> decrypt_file SUCCEEDS and
    writes the plaintext WITHOUT it, silently.
That asymmetry is filed separately rather than fixed here -- see the new ticket
referenced below.

VERDICT: not solvable today, and not by this lane at any point, because the
write half has no implementation to reach for. Recommend closing as
documented-not-fixed and reopening only if YAML::PP ships its parse tree.

